# Stories Flow

## Backend — Content Types

### `api::story.story` (`story_seens` table)
| Field | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `Title` | string, required | PascalCase → `title` column |
| `Slug` | uid → Title | auto-generated |
| `IsActive` | boolean, default false | `is_active` column |
| `SortOrder` | integer, default 0 | `sort_order` column |
| `MediaType` | enum: image \| video | `media_type` column |
| `Media` | media (images, videos) | |
| `Thumbnail` | media (images) | for video stories |
| `StartAt` | datetime | schedule start |
| `EndAt` | datetime | schedule end |
| `DurationMs` | integer, default 5000 | `duration_ms` column |
| `CtaLabel` | string, max 60 | `cta_label` column |
| `CtaUrl` | string, max 500 | `cta_url` column |
| `Overlays` | json | array of `StoryOverlay` objects |

### `api::story-seen.story-seen` (`story_seens` table)
| Field | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `story` | manyToOne → story | inverse: `story_seens` |
| `user` | manyToOne → plugin::users-permissions.user | NOT local-user |
| `SeenAt` | datetime, required | |

## API Endpoints

| Method | Path | Auth | Handler |
|---|---|---|---|
| GET | `/api/stories` | public | core find |
| GET | `/api/stories/active` | public | `story.getActive` |
| GET | `/api/stories/:id` | public | core findOne |
| POST | `/api/stories` | superadmin/store-manager | core create |
| PUT | `/api/stories/:id` | superadmin/store-manager | core update |
| DELETE | `/api/stories/:id` | superadmin/store-manager | core delete |
| POST | `/api/story-seens/mark` | customer+ | `story-seen.markSeen` |
| GET | `/api/story-seens/mine` | customer+ | `story-seen.getMine` |

## `getActive` Filter Logic

```typescript
filters: {
  IsActive: true,
  $or: [{ StartAt: { $null: true } }, { StartAt: { $lte: now } }],
  $and: [{ $or: [{ EndAt: { $null: true } }, { EndAt: { $gte: now } }] }],
}
sort: { SortOrder: "asc" }
```

## Seen Idempotency

`markSeen` in `story-seen.service.ts` uses **create-once** logic:
1. `findOne({ where: { user: userId, story: storyId } })`
2. If exists → return `{ created: false }` — no duplicate created
3. If not → create with `SeenAt: new Date()`

Never add a unique DB constraint for V1 (no race-condition handling needed at this scale).

## Permission Grants (`backend/src/index.ts`)

```typescript
// public
"api::story": { story: ["find", "findOne", "getActive"] }

// customer (inherits public)
"api::story-seen": { "story-seen": ["markSeen", "getMine"] }

// editor / store-manager / superadmin: mode: "all" (already covers everything)
```

## Auth Pattern

Always use `plugin::users-permissions.user` (NOT `local-user`) for user relations in seen tracking. Access via `ctx.state.user.id` in controllers.

## Persian Error Messages

All backend error responses must be Persian. Examples from `story` controller:
- `ctx.forbidden("شما مجاز به ایجاد استوری نیستید.")`
- `ctx.notFound("استوری یافت نشد.")`
- `ctx.unauthorized("برای ثبت مشاهده باید وارد حساب کاربری خود شوید.")`
- `ctx.internalServerError("خطا در دریافت استوری‌ها. دوباره تلاش کنید.")`

Add frontend translations to `frontend/src/lib/errorTranslations.ts` → `ERROR_MESSAGE_MAP`.

## Frontend Service

File: `frontend/src/services/story/story.service.ts`

| Function | Auth | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `getActiveStories()` | public | SSR-safe; uses `getStrapiServerUrl()` + `fetch()` with `next: { revalidate: 60 }` |
| `getMySeenStoryIds()` | authenticated | uses `apiClient.get` |
| `markStorySeen(storyId)` | authenticated | idempotent |
| `listStories(params)` | admin | pagination, search, isActive filter |
| `getStory(id)` | admin | single story |
| `createStory(data)` | admin | |
| `updateStory(id, data)` | admin | |
| `deleteStory(id)` | admin | |

Endpoints are registered in `frontend/src/constants/api.ts` → `ENDPOINTS.STORIES`.

## Seen State Hook

`frontend/src/hooks/useStoriesSeenState.ts`
- **Guests**: localStorage (`story_seen_ids` key) only
- **Authenticated**: merges server IDs on mount, calls API on each `markSeen`
- Returns `{ seenIds, markSeen, hasSeen }`

## Homepage Integration

`frontend/src/app/(product)/page.tsx`:
- `getStoriesForHome()` added to `Promise.all` block
- `<StoriesRail stories={activeStories} />` renders after hero, before `<HomeProductSections>`
- Hidden when `activeStories.length === 0`

## Story Viewer Library

Package: `react-instagram-stories`
- Import styles in `globals.css` before Tailwind: `@import 'react-instagram-stories/styles.css'`
- `User` shape: `{ id: string, username: string, avatarUrl: string, stories: StoryItem[], hasUnreadStories?: boolean }`
- Our mapping: each `Story` → one `User` with one `StoryItem` (image or video)
- `hasUnreadStories = !seenIds.has(story.id)` — drives the ring indicator
- Use **controlled mode** (`isOpen`, `onClose`, `onStoryChange`) to avoid URL param conflicts
